WEBVTT

00:41.875 --> 00:46.963
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

02:48.543 --> 02:49.544
What happened?

02:58.428 --> 03:00.513
What happened next?

03:06.019 --> 03:07.437
Can you guess who it is?

03:08.104 --> 03:09.772
Someone who's close to you

03:10.523 --> 03:12.442
and knows you…

03:15.695 --> 03:18.698
The waveform analysis indicates
a woman in her twenties.

03:22.994 --> 03:24.329
Compare it with 406.

03:24.871 --> 03:26.789
See how much they match in percentage.

03:26.873 --> 03:28.124
Up to two decimal places.

03:32.670 --> 03:34.547
EPISODE 6

04:02.533 --> 04:03.368
Why…

04:04.953 --> 04:07.956
were we lying on the floor together
last night?

04:12.252 --> 04:14.295
What? What is it?

04:21.886 --> 04:23.096
What is it?

04:23.721 --> 04:26.474
Tell me if something happened.

04:36.651 --> 04:38.695
Should I tell you everything honestly?

04:40.613 --> 04:41.447
Honest…

04:42.532 --> 04:44.367
"Tell you everything honestly"?

05:22.113 --> 05:24.490
PARK DO-JAE

05:28.036 --> 05:28.870
Yes?

05:28.953 --> 05:29.787
Mr. Paik.

05:30.580 --> 05:31.622
What happened?

05:31.706 --> 05:33.541
Your phone was off. I was worried.

05:34.625 --> 05:35.918
I'm sorry.

05:36.002 --> 05:37.003
It just happened.

05:37.754 --> 05:39.589
As for the favor I asked for yesterday?

05:39.672 --> 05:40.840
Did you not see it?

05:41.632 --> 05:43.342
I sent you a text last night.

05:43.968 --> 05:45.219
But you never responded.

06:02.070 --> 06:06.657
It's a 99.99% match.

06:10.787 --> 06:12.955
I made a summary of all the events so far.

06:13.039 --> 06:14.791
From the first threatening call

06:14.874 --> 06:17.543
to the recent incident
at the nursing home.

06:17.627 --> 06:18.878
I came to one conclusion.

06:18.961 --> 06:20.671
The caller, 406, isn't involved

06:20.755 --> 06:23.591
in the kidnapping, explosion,
and nursing home incident.

06:23.674 --> 06:24.634
There's someone else.

06:26.427 --> 06:27.678
I know that.

06:28.387 --> 06:29.722
They're not accomplices.

06:31.766 --> 06:34.936
You have an idea who 406 might be,
don't you?

06:35.019 --> 06:36.187
I'm sorry.

06:36.938 --> 06:38.648
I can't tell you right now.

06:39.315 --> 06:43.653
For now, let's find the connection
between him and 406 and break it.

06:45.113 --> 06:46.364
After that…

06:47.615 --> 06:48.449
Are you okay?

06:50.076 --> 06:51.077
You don't look well.

06:53.496 --> 06:54.497
I'm fine.

06:57.125 --> 06:58.042
Yes, sir.

06:58.960 --> 07:00.211
If you need anything--

07:00.294 --> 07:01.337
No.

07:02.839 --> 07:03.923
I'm not okay.

07:09.595 --> 07:10.888
You see,

07:12.431 --> 07:15.351
I thought
I'd controlled situations perfectly

07:15.435 --> 07:17.520
and made better judgments than anyone.

07:18.604 --> 07:20.857
I thought I had lived meticulously

07:22.608 --> 07:25.111
not to fall into any traps.

07:29.323 --> 07:30.450
But…

07:31.242 --> 07:32.577
why didn't I know?

07:33.870 --> 07:34.787
When I think back,

07:35.621 --> 07:37.623
there were more than a few hints.

07:39.375 --> 07:42.462
Maybe I just ignored them.

07:43.337 --> 07:45.756
I firmly believed it couldn't be true,

07:45.840 --> 07:48.176
desperately hoping it wasn't.

07:49.552 --> 07:51.137
But I shouldn't have done that.

07:51.971 --> 07:54.098
I should've at least prepared myself.

07:54.974 --> 07:56.225
If I had,

07:56.309 --> 07:59.729
I wouldn't be at a loss for what to do.

08:02.690 --> 08:04.525
You have until tomorrow to decide.

08:05.276 --> 08:07.278
Or we can settle for two billion won.

08:07.361 --> 08:08.529
You have until tomorrow.

08:08.613 --> 08:10.656
It's not like you married her for love.

08:10.740 --> 08:12.283
You don't even love her now.

08:12.366 --> 08:14.118
If it's going to be like that,

08:15.912 --> 08:17.538
just leave her.

08:24.754 --> 08:25.588
THE SEVENTH CALL

08:25.671 --> 08:28.382
Then why did you treat her
like she was invisible?

08:38.142 --> 08:39.477
THE THIRD CALL

08:39.560 --> 08:40.811
It's Hong Hee-joo's…

08:45.733 --> 08:46.984
thigh.

08:52.114 --> 08:54.200
You're supposed to be her husband.

08:54.825 --> 08:57.662
Didn't you know
Hee-joo has a unique mole on her thigh?

08:58.412 --> 09:00.331
How could you not know?

09:00.915 --> 09:03.000
Were you just not interested? Or…

09:04.961 --> 09:06.462
have you never seen her naked?

09:15.263 --> 09:16.097
Enough.

09:55.845 --> 09:57.054
It grew longer as I wrote.

09:58.639 --> 10:00.433
100 QUESTIONS, 100 ANSWERS

10:03.978 --> 10:05.980
Wait. I forgot one.

10:11.360 --> 10:13.321
LIES, ANGER, HATRED,
MISUNDERSTANDING, FORGIVENESS

10:13.404 --> 10:14.780
What's the sign language

10:15.364 --> 10:16.282
for forgiveness?

10:24.874 --> 10:28.336
What about "I forgive your wrongdoings"?

10:59.033 --> 11:00.076
It's difficult.

11:01.202 --> 11:02.036
Forgiveness.

11:06.666 --> 11:08.250
Let's end today's class here.

11:36.779 --> 11:39.907
YOU DIDN'T TEXT BACK,
SO I'M TEXTING AGAIN. LET'S MEET UP TODAY.

11:50.709 --> 11:52.294
SIGN LANGUAGE

11:58.134 --> 12:01.887
The pre-candidate registration
for the 21st presidential election,

12:01.971 --> 12:05.141
which will be held in March next year,
will begin next week.

12:05.891 --> 12:07.309
Sir.

12:07.393 --> 12:10.146
It's about the task
you asked me to check regularly.

12:10.229 --> 12:14.150
Regarding Chairman Hong Il-gyeong's
eldest daughter, Hong In-a.

12:46.265 --> 12:47.141
Honey.

12:47.224 --> 12:50.227
Chairman Hong's eldest daughter
is back in Korea.

12:52.855 --> 12:53.939
So what?

12:54.023 --> 12:56.108
What do you mean?

12:56.192 --> 12:58.235
You should meet with her.

12:58.319 --> 13:00.738
And ask her why she caused that mess.

13:00.821 --> 13:03.657
No, before that, see if we can control…

13:04.867 --> 13:05.993
Are you drinking?

13:08.162 --> 13:09.246
Are you drunk?

13:11.749 --> 13:13.083
Can't I be drunk?

13:14.335 --> 13:15.586
On a day like today?

13:17.129 --> 13:18.088
What's today?

13:20.257 --> 13:21.091
What is it?

13:25.971 --> 13:27.306
A day no one can remember.

13:28.474 --> 13:31.435
A day that shouldn't be remembered.

13:32.186 --> 13:35.022
That's what your father decided.

13:35.105 --> 13:36.106
So what?

13:38.150 --> 13:41.654
Why? Must you pretend to care?

13:42.238 --> 13:44.823
Would that ease your guilt a little?

13:45.699 --> 13:46.867
Don't make me laugh.

13:47.576 --> 13:49.620
Twenty years ago today,

13:49.703 --> 13:52.540
both you and I know how we really felt!

13:55.793 --> 13:56.627
What?

13:59.797 --> 14:01.131
A sense of freedom.

15:05.362 --> 15:07.740
IS IT IMPOSSIBLE
TO CHANGE INNATE TEMPERAMENT?

15:42.900 --> 15:44.151
Goodness.

15:44.234 --> 15:45.402
You must be In-a.

15:46.528 --> 15:48.489
How dare you touch me
with your filthy hands?

16:56.849 --> 16:57.975
Hee-joo.

17:03.313 --> 17:04.606
How have you been?

17:11.071 --> 17:12.072
Do you remember?

17:12.740 --> 17:14.783
We'd visit the aquarium often as kids.

17:15.743 --> 17:18.912
It felt like all the sounds
in the world disappeared

17:20.456 --> 17:22.833
when I stared into the water like this.

17:23.792 --> 17:25.294
It made me feel at peace.

17:27.880 --> 17:29.465
Let's see the mermaid show you like.

17:30.049 --> 17:30.883
It starts soon.

17:32.426 --> 17:33.343
Isn't it amazing?

17:33.927 --> 17:35.721
Hearing me chattering like this.

17:36.430 --> 17:38.098
I must've been lucky.

17:38.182 --> 17:40.100
The surgery was a success.

17:40.184 --> 17:43.228
No surgery could fix me when I was young.

17:49.151 --> 17:50.486
But, Hee-joo…

17:52.946 --> 17:54.490
why are you still the same?

17:55.824 --> 17:57.367
You can talk now.

17:58.035 --> 17:59.620
You don't need to keep quiet.

18:08.212 --> 18:10.756
You knew?

18:11.548 --> 18:12.382
Yeah.

18:14.510 --> 18:16.011
You didn't speak…

18:18.263 --> 18:19.640
because of me.

18:29.358 --> 18:30.609
I know.

18:31.401 --> 18:33.278
I did a terrible thing to you.

18:33.904 --> 18:35.739
I know it was awful of me,

18:37.533 --> 18:39.409
but I didn't want to fall apart alone.

18:40.244 --> 18:42.037
I needed someone to be miserable

18:43.914 --> 18:44.998
with me.

18:47.793 --> 18:48.794
Hee-joo.

18:50.754 --> 18:51.672
So what?

18:51.755 --> 18:54.550
Now that you're okay,
are you allowing me to speak?

18:56.218 --> 18:57.928
No, that's not up to you.

18:59.012 --> 19:00.389
I'll decide it.

19:00.889 --> 19:02.808
I won't let you interfere
in my life anymore.

19:05.060 --> 19:06.895
You don't know what I'm saying, do you?

19:06.979 --> 19:08.147
It doesn't matter.

19:08.230 --> 19:10.732
I'll say what I want,
just like what you're doing.

19:14.903 --> 19:17.197
THE LITTLE MERMAID'S MYSTERIOUS ADVENTURE

19:20.242 --> 19:22.077
I don't like The Little Mermaid.

19:22.786 --> 19:23.620
I hate her.

19:44.516 --> 19:46.185
IN-A

20:00.908 --> 20:01.742
Hee-joo.

20:02.826 --> 20:05.287
I needed to tell you something today.

20:05.370 --> 20:08.707
Do you think you know Paik Sa-eon well?

20:14.254 --> 20:17.382
Before the wedding,
I didn't dump you on him.

20:17.466 --> 20:19.301
He asked for you.

20:19.384 --> 20:21.386
In return for letting me go,

20:21.929 --> 20:24.223
he needed a connection to our family,

20:24.306 --> 20:25.724
so he took you hostage.

20:33.982 --> 20:35.651
I came to one conclusion.

20:36.235 --> 20:37.819
The caller, 406, isn't involved

20:37.903 --> 20:40.697
in the kidnapping, explosion,
and nursing home incident.

20:40.781 --> 20:41.740
There's someone else.

22:04.197 --> 22:05.115
It's just…

22:05.824 --> 22:07.743
My phone's missing.

22:08.577 --> 22:10.120
Why is he looking for that here?

22:13.457 --> 22:14.875
CALLS
PAIK SA-EON

22:32.601 --> 22:33.435
Wait.

22:34.311 --> 22:35.145
What's this?

22:40.108 --> 22:41.276
So Hee-joo was…

22:42.861 --> 22:44.529
into this kind of thing?

23:27.864 --> 23:28.865
Did I…

23:30.867 --> 23:31.701
I mean,

23:32.953 --> 23:33.787
did we…

23:35.705 --> 23:36.540
by any chance…

24:20.250 --> 24:22.169
I must be insane.

25:00.332 --> 25:01.666
How did you know?

25:03.043 --> 25:04.002
About what?

25:04.085 --> 25:07.005
That I've been thinking about you
all day long.

25:07.964 --> 25:10.050
We spoke on the phone every day.

25:10.759 --> 25:14.262
But there are still so many things
I don't know about you.

25:16.473 --> 25:18.308
So now I want to know more.

25:19.392 --> 25:20.477
Then…

25:21.436 --> 25:24.606
how about we each
ask a question and answer?

25:24.689 --> 25:25.523
Sounds good.

25:26.191 --> 25:27.651
However, from this moment on,

25:28.526 --> 25:30.362
we'll only speak the truth.

25:31.071 --> 25:32.030
That's what I want.

25:33.615 --> 25:34.783
Go ahead.

25:35.700 --> 25:37.202
The day before the wedding,

25:37.911 --> 25:40.247
you said you met In-a and made a deal.

25:42.791 --> 25:45.126
Was the deal about Hong Hee-joo?

25:45.210 --> 25:46.044
Yes.

25:47.295 --> 25:48.213
It's my turn.

25:49.005 --> 25:51.591
What? My question isn't over yet.

25:51.675 --> 25:53.134
I answered, so it's over.

25:53.218 --> 25:55.637
Think carefully next time before you ask.

25:56.763 --> 25:57.973
It's my turn.

25:58.056 --> 26:01.810
Is Hong Hee-joo being threatened
right now?

26:03.061 --> 26:05.230
Why do you think she's being threatened?

26:05.313 --> 26:07.399
406, you kidnapped Hee-joo

26:07.482 --> 26:09.317
and even attacked her father.

26:09.401 --> 26:11.069
You're completely insane.

26:13.238 --> 26:14.572
Hee-joo would never side

26:15.282 --> 26:16.741
with someone like you.

26:18.285 --> 26:21.788
She's being threatened,
but also not, okay?

26:22.831 --> 26:23.832
It's my turn now.

26:24.457 --> 26:26.293
Did you take Hong Hee-joo hostage

26:26.376 --> 26:29.504
in exchange for letting Hong In-a
go free from the arranged marriage?

26:31.589 --> 26:32.799
Who told you that?

26:33.383 --> 26:36.052
Seeing how you're asking that,
I guess it's true.

26:37.804 --> 26:38.638
It's true.

26:40.432 --> 26:41.349
I…

26:41.891 --> 26:43.935
often have nightmares.

26:44.602 --> 26:46.521
I had them more often as a kid.

27:14.758 --> 27:15.884
I will

27:16.718 --> 27:17.552
help you.

27:18.428 --> 27:21.139
I will be with you.

27:23.892 --> 27:24.893
It's okay.

27:25.894 --> 27:26.853
It's okay.

27:44.871 --> 27:45.705
It's okay.

27:52.629 --> 27:53.588
It's okay.

27:54.172 --> 27:56.007
What calmed me down every time…

27:57.967 --> 27:59.886
were the gestures of the girl next door

28:01.638 --> 28:03.640
who practiced sign language every night.

28:06.101 --> 28:07.602
But that girl

28:09.020 --> 28:10.105
had no one

28:11.398 --> 28:13.066
to rely on, anywhere.

28:14.776 --> 28:16.194
Because to her,

28:17.821 --> 28:20.240
Chairman Hong's house was a prison.

28:22.075 --> 28:24.244
I wanted to help her escape.

28:25.120 --> 28:26.454
Hoping that she could

28:27.789 --> 28:29.707
leave that house and live freely.

28:31.584 --> 28:33.002
But I never imagined…

28:35.004 --> 28:36.089
that I would become…

28:37.757 --> 28:39.259
Hee-joo's new prison.

28:40.260 --> 28:41.469
Prison?

28:43.054 --> 28:44.305
A married life with me

28:45.223 --> 28:47.058
after leaving that house

28:48.768 --> 28:51.438
must've felt like a prison to her.

28:52.397 --> 28:55.233
That must be why she got mixed up
with some crazy person

28:55.859 --> 28:58.027
in order to divorce me, right?

29:01.114 --> 29:02.365
It's my turn now.

29:04.451 --> 29:05.785
Does Hong Hee-joo…

29:07.412 --> 29:08.830
still want a divorce?

29:14.753 --> 29:16.004
Answer me, 406.

29:16.755 --> 29:18.465
Isn't that what you kept saying?

29:18.548 --> 29:21.384
To let Hee-joo go
and return things to the way they were.

29:23.136 --> 29:24.387
To let go of her.

29:28.016 --> 29:30.310
She didn't want
to get her hopes up anymore.

29:31.478 --> 29:32.687
"Someday,

29:34.606 --> 29:35.857
things will change."

29:37.942 --> 29:41.696
"It'll get better."
She waited and hoped for three years.

29:42.489 --> 29:43.573
If you let her go,

29:44.699 --> 29:46.367
she thought she wouldn't get hurt

29:47.202 --> 29:49.996
or be disappointed anymore.

29:50.079 --> 29:52.373
That's what Hong Hee-joo thought.

29:52.457 --> 29:53.708
By any chance,

29:55.543 --> 29:56.836
does Hee-joo want…

30:00.423 --> 30:01.424
SINCERITY

30:01.508 --> 30:02.592
sincerity,

30:04.010 --> 30:05.386
attention,

30:05.470 --> 30:06.679
understanding,

30:07.388 --> 30:08.306
and affection?

30:09.224 --> 30:10.391
Is that what she wants?

30:12.519 --> 30:14.479
What are you saying? What I'm saying--

30:14.562 --> 30:15.897
I can give that to her.

30:21.486 --> 30:22.904
I can give her everything.

30:26.241 --> 30:29.828
If that's what Hee-joo wants,
I'll give as much as she needs.

30:31.204 --> 30:33.039
Why do you suddenly want to do that?

30:35.750 --> 30:37.794
You didn't care whether I lived or died,

30:37.877 --> 30:40.129
or whether I was by your side, until now.

30:41.089 --> 30:42.090
From the very start,

30:44.926 --> 30:47.011
this wasn't a marriage Hee-joo wanted.

30:48.054 --> 30:50.265
I kept her by my side as a hostage,

30:52.183 --> 30:53.768
thinking that someday…

30:54.769 --> 30:56.354
I'd have to let her go.

30:58.648 --> 31:00.650
Is that why you were so cruel?

31:01.860 --> 31:03.069
So you wouldn't get attached?

31:03.820 --> 31:05.405
But if that's what Hee-joo wants,

31:06.573 --> 31:07.574
it changes things.

31:10.493 --> 31:11.494
Then promise me.

31:12.620 --> 31:13.746
If I make an effort

31:15.248 --> 31:16.708
and we can change,

31:17.834 --> 31:20.795
promise you'll never make this call again.

31:26.926 --> 31:28.344
That depends on how you act.

32:11.095 --> 32:12.180
Oh, my, ma'am.

32:12.972 --> 32:15.558
You look so young and beautiful today.

32:16.225 --> 32:17.435
Of course.

32:17.518 --> 32:19.896
My age may increase,
but my skirt length shouldn't.

32:19.979 --> 32:21.064
Of course.

32:22.815 --> 32:24.734
Can't you dress a bit younger too?

32:26.486 --> 32:28.738
Why should I have to struggle
to look younger?

32:31.491 --> 32:32.575
You're right.

32:32.659 --> 32:34.160
It wouldn't suit you.

32:34.243 --> 32:37.038
You already have a gorgeous charm
about you.

32:41.167 --> 32:42.627
Okay, then.

32:42.710 --> 32:44.295
Get in. Good luck today.

32:45.880 --> 32:47.715
Let's go. Okay.

33:05.358 --> 33:07.026
How much is Spokesperson Paik asking for?

33:07.110 --> 33:07.944
What?

33:08.027 --> 33:09.487
What's his price?

33:10.071 --> 33:11.322
Good luck with the negotiation.

33:11.406 --> 33:12.865
Between parents and children,

33:13.408 --> 33:15.243
there should be
some playful give-and-take.

33:15.326 --> 33:16.160
I don't know.

33:17.328 --> 33:19.747
Don't you know as well as I do?

33:20.581 --> 33:22.667
Getting a stubborn child to listen

33:23.835 --> 33:25.503
is harder than practicing discipline.

33:26.295 --> 33:28.047
Your eldest daughter.

33:29.173 --> 33:30.675
Do you know how she's doing?

33:32.176 --> 33:34.470
Why would you suddenly bring her up?

33:35.680 --> 33:37.348
She comes to mind lately.

33:38.141 --> 33:41.144
I wonder how she's doing.

33:48.484 --> 33:51.863
- Are you ready for this?
- I've never been to a retreat before.

33:51.946 --> 33:54.157
- I've organized this well.
- I am a little nervous.

33:54.240 --> 33:56.284
Is that like your security pillow?

33:57.118 --> 33:59.954
So only Mr. Paik and Mr. Park
aren't here yet?

34:00.038 --> 34:01.789
- Should I call them?
- Nah.

34:01.873 --> 34:03.916
What? What's that?

34:05.001 --> 34:06.127
What is that?

34:06.210 --> 34:07.628
THANK YOU, SPOKESPERSON'S TEAM

34:08.880 --> 34:10.214
WHEEL LUNCHBOX

34:11.007 --> 34:13.885
TO THE SPOKESPERSON'S TEAM, THANK YOU

34:14.552 --> 34:15.553
Let's go.

34:20.850 --> 34:22.852
The staff from the spokesperson's office?

34:22.935 --> 34:25.021
- Yes.
- The lunchboxes have arrived.

34:28.441 --> 34:29.567
- Thank you.
- Here you go.

34:30.193 --> 34:31.360
Pass these out.

34:31.444 --> 34:32.653
Take that.

34:34.113 --> 34:35.073
Thank you.

34:36.032 --> 34:37.075
Goodness.

34:38.576 --> 34:41.120
- Do you have mine?
- Goodness.

34:41.204 --> 34:42.371
Look at the hearts.

34:43.581 --> 34:45.917
"An office full of love."

34:46.000 --> 34:47.877
Is that what this is, Mr. Kang?

34:47.960 --> 34:50.004
It wasn't me. I didn't order these.

34:50.088 --> 34:51.339
Who sent these?

34:52.173 --> 34:53.007
I don't know.

34:54.717 --> 34:56.344
Is everyone here?

34:56.427 --> 34:58.513
- Hello.
- Hello.

35:01.182 --> 35:03.768
The lunchboxes came too.

35:03.851 --> 35:07.271
Wait, did you order these, sir?

35:14.320 --> 35:17.115
- Let's go.
- Wait…

35:17.949 --> 35:19.742
- What?
- What's going on?

35:19.826 --> 35:22.453
- Let… Let's go.
- What?

35:22.537 --> 35:24.413
Look at this heart.

35:24.497 --> 35:27.208
I didn't know
he'd prepare lunchboxes for us.

35:50.731 --> 35:51.732
Is this seat taken?

35:58.489 --> 35:59.365
Do you want one?

36:09.584 --> 36:10.418
I get…

36:11.544 --> 36:12.962
carsick.

36:14.046 --> 36:17.258
Doesn't it get worse
if you sit in the back?

36:17.925 --> 36:20.428
Right. Then why don't you sit there?

36:21.929 --> 36:24.974
I think I'll leave my things here.

36:25.057 --> 36:25.892
I see.

36:26.893 --> 36:28.686
Then would you like to sit here?

36:31.147 --> 36:31.981
Thank you.

36:39.989 --> 36:40.990
Coffee…

36:41.991 --> 36:44.076
isn't good on an empty stomach, Ms. Hong.

36:51.667 --> 36:52.543
Proof?

36:53.794 --> 36:56.255
Are we cops or something?
How can we find proof?

36:57.548 --> 36:58.549
A witness?

37:01.177 --> 37:03.137
There's no proof.
How would we find a witness?

37:03.846 --> 37:06.349
Not to mention,
these kids don't have a family.

37:07.516 --> 37:09.852
It's in the development stage.
If we keep digging…

37:11.103 --> 37:12.897
Hello?

37:12.980 --> 37:14.065
Mr. Han?

37:15.775 --> 37:16.692
What?

37:16.776 --> 37:18.194
He just hung up on me.

37:18.903 --> 37:19.904
Do they want to toss it?

37:21.364 --> 37:23.824
- Well…
- "If the NeoTuber's story is fake,

37:23.908 --> 37:25.243
will you take responsibility?"

37:25.326 --> 37:26.994
Why would I take responsibility?

37:27.078 --> 37:27.954
You have to.

37:29.914 --> 37:31.707
Why are you helping so enthusiastically?

37:32.333 --> 37:33.376
Because…

37:37.088 --> 37:38.464
Why are you buying so much?

37:39.423 --> 37:40.299
It's not that much.

37:41.175 --> 37:44.178
At least for hungry little ones
whose stomachs can never be filled.

37:45.638 --> 37:47.723
I'm a huge fan of hers!

37:47.807 --> 37:49.392
I need to get her autograph.

37:50.726 --> 37:51.727
I don't believe it.

37:51.811 --> 37:53.813
Thank you so much.

37:54.522 --> 37:56.857
- Hello!
- Cool.

37:58.109 --> 37:59.694
Thank you.

38:02.196 --> 38:04.615
Are you Dr. Sang-woo's girlfriend?

38:05.116 --> 38:06.325
What?

38:06.409 --> 38:07.702
Want to see his dark past?

38:07.785 --> 38:10.371
If you still like him after,
it's real love.

38:10.454 --> 38:13.541
No, wait.
I'm not Dr. Sang-woo's girlfriend.

38:28.139 --> 38:30.308
Guys, let's eat!

38:33.728 --> 38:34.729
Be careful.

38:34.812 --> 38:36.480
Be careful.

38:41.235 --> 38:42.570
Let's eat.

38:43.654 --> 38:45.072
No, you can't look!

38:45.156 --> 38:46.532
Wait! Hey!

38:46.615 --> 38:48.617
Hey! This isn't right.

38:56.834 --> 38:57.668
This picture…

38:59.754 --> 39:04.342
I heard the kids started disappearing
around this time.

39:04.425 --> 39:05.926
This was before you came here.

39:06.886 --> 39:08.095
Do you know anything?

39:08.804 --> 39:10.389
No, I don't.

39:10.473 --> 39:13.059
Did any of the birth parents come back
later on?

39:17.980 --> 39:22.360
So, the missing kids
had no family searching for them

39:24.570 --> 39:27.198
and no one to remember them all this time.

39:30.785 --> 39:34.705
Shin Yeong-seok liked to play marbles,
and he was so competitive.

39:36.248 --> 39:38.626
Lee Jin-yeong liked cars.

39:38.709 --> 39:40.961
Park Min-woo. He was so…

39:42.588 --> 39:43.589
Such a troublemaker.

39:44.840 --> 39:45.758
I remember them.

39:48.177 --> 39:49.053
These three.

39:51.722 --> 39:52.723
That's strange.

39:53.557 --> 39:54.725
I heard

39:55.476 --> 39:57.978
that four kids disappeared.

39:58.062 --> 39:59.522
There's one more?

40:00.022 --> 40:01.816
Yes, here.

40:06.404 --> 40:08.030
One of the twin brothers.

40:36.517 --> 40:39.103
CHANGE OF PLAN. TODAY'S D-DAY.

42:40.432 --> 42:41.267
Hey, honey.

42:43.185 --> 42:44.144
No, I wasn't sleeping.

42:44.228 --> 42:46.397
Is it hard on your own?
Sorry, I couldn't go.

42:48.023 --> 42:48.857
What?

42:52.403 --> 42:53.237
Yeah.

42:54.863 --> 42:57.157
I love you,
my ultimate love in the universe!

42:57.241 --> 42:58.993
Park Eun-yeong, I love you so much!

43:10.129 --> 43:11.297
I apologize.

43:21.932 --> 43:23.934
How do you do that?

43:24.018 --> 43:24.852
Excuse me?

43:26.103 --> 43:27.688
What you just did.

43:28.731 --> 43:30.941
"I love you,
ultimate love in the universe."

43:31.025 --> 43:32.109
You're good at that.

43:32.192 --> 43:33.027
You know,

43:33.819 --> 43:36.405
it's only hard at first,
but it gets easier to do.

43:36.488 --> 43:40.743
Think of it as adding a little flavor
to the affection you usually show.

43:40.826 --> 43:42.077
Say it with a kiss.

43:45.789 --> 43:46.790
Wait,

43:48.459 --> 43:49.960
you do show affection, right?

43:56.383 --> 43:58.302
You've been married for about…

43:58.385 --> 43:59.219
Three years.

44:00.721 --> 44:02.640
You're practically newlyweds. So why?

44:05.684 --> 44:08.437
You know, time sure does fly.

44:08.520 --> 44:11.690
It feels like I got married yesterday,
but it's already been ten years.

44:12.399 --> 44:14.568
Time flies by so quickly,

44:15.194 --> 44:16.612
what's the use of saving it?

44:17.738 --> 44:20.491
When she's by your side,
tell her you love her

44:21.325 --> 44:22.326
and thank her

44:23.452 --> 44:24.536
as much as you can.

44:44.890 --> 44:47.810
We've unpacked and warmed up now.

44:47.893 --> 44:49.937
Thank you for the lunchboxes, Mr. Paik!

44:50.020 --> 44:50.854
Thank you.

44:50.938 --> 44:53.941
Now that we're full,
shall we start the sports competition?

44:54.024 --> 44:54.983
Gosh.

44:55.067 --> 44:57.236
Someone stop Mr. Kang.

44:57.319 --> 45:00.072
Yeah. Who knew he was so into events?

45:00.155 --> 45:03.409
All events will be played in pairs.

45:03.492 --> 45:06.495
The teams will be
the spokespersons versus the interpreters.

45:06.578 --> 45:08.288
Let's team up, Hee-joo.

45:09.248 --> 45:10.541
No.

45:10.624 --> 45:14.044
We came to build a rapport
with the interpreters.

45:14.128 --> 45:17.423
What's the point of this retreat
if you arrange the teams like that?

45:18.465 --> 45:19.550
Shall we mix them, perhaps?

45:19.633 --> 45:22.344
Mr. Paik, why don't you pick
one of the interpreters first…

45:22.428 --> 45:23.637
Okay.

45:29.518 --> 45:31.520
Let's team up, Ms. Hong.

45:31.603 --> 45:34.273
Then, that's one team!

45:35.149 --> 45:38.068
- Good luck.
- Everyone else can team up too.

45:38.777 --> 45:40.028
What's the prize?

45:41.488 --> 45:43.532
- The winning team--
- Let them pick.

45:43.615 --> 45:46.743
- Excuse me?
- The winning team can pick their prize.

45:47.494 --> 45:48.328
Let's start.

45:49.663 --> 45:50.581
What they want!

45:51.248 --> 45:52.332
Warm up.

46:00.424 --> 46:02.676
The first event is just a warm-up.

46:02.759 --> 46:05.220
We'll start with
a two-person jump rope challenge!

46:05.929 --> 46:06.763
Now.

46:06.847 --> 46:10.726
There's a lot of room for mistakes
in this event, so you'll get two chances.

46:10.809 --> 46:13.854
We'll start with Park Do-jae
and Kim Tae-kyeong.

46:13.937 --> 46:15.397
- Okay, spin it.
- Good luck.

46:20.944 --> 46:21.778
Here I go.

46:21.862 --> 46:22.696
That was good.

46:22.779 --> 46:23.614
That's good!

46:23.697 --> 46:25.282
Nice!

46:25.365 --> 46:28.118
I'll go in first.
Make sure to time it right and jump.

46:28.202 --> 46:31.121
Speed, reflexes, timing, and focus
are all important.

46:31.205 --> 46:32.414
Mr. Park, you look so calm.

46:32.498 --> 46:34.124
Seven, eight!

46:34.208 --> 46:35.709
That's too bad.

46:35.792 --> 46:36.627
How many?

46:36.710 --> 46:38.629
That makes it seven.

46:38.712 --> 46:39.713
- Now, next.
- Good job.

46:39.796 --> 46:40.631
Okay, next.

46:40.714 --> 46:41.840
Mr. Paik's team.

46:45.385 --> 46:46.220
Come on.

46:50.682 --> 46:51.558
One.

46:52.351 --> 46:53.560
Are you okay?

46:53.644 --> 46:55.729
- Take it easy.
- That's zero.

46:56.563 --> 46:57.648
Mr. Paik, you're out!

46:59.900 --> 47:01.026
I'm sorry.

47:05.322 --> 47:06.907
Once again. Next.

47:07.491 --> 47:08.951
It's smooth this time.

47:09.034 --> 47:10.661
Now.

47:10.744 --> 47:12.454
I've figured out the trick.

47:12.538 --> 47:13.914
I can do a good job this time.

47:13.997 --> 47:16.875
Once I find the rhythm after a few jumps,
then you can--

47:17.501 --> 47:18.418
Are you listening?

47:18.502 --> 47:20.420
I'll go first. Just follow me.

47:21.046 --> 47:22.673
Twelve.

47:22.756 --> 47:24.174
How many was that?

47:24.258 --> 47:26.009
- It's 12 this time.
- Okay.

47:26.093 --> 47:28.220
Okay, let's get Mr. Paik's team.
Team Paik?

47:35.602 --> 47:37.062
- Now!
- There you go! Okay!

47:41.066 --> 47:42.985
- You have to go.
- Go, Mr. Paik!

47:43.068 --> 47:45.153
We'll count once Mr. Paik comes in.

48:20.314 --> 48:22.232
We finally found one.

48:22.316 --> 48:23.442
The victim's family.

48:24.109 --> 48:28.071
If his little brother is alive
and if he was looking for his brother,

48:29.072 --> 48:31.074
then he may know something.

48:31.992 --> 48:33.160
I know.

48:33.243 --> 48:34.578
But…

48:34.661 --> 48:37.789
it won't be easy to figure out
where he is or how he's living.

48:37.873 --> 48:41.793
Well, the director said that
the old documents were lost or discarded

48:41.877 --> 48:43.420
when the operating foundation changed.

48:43.503 --> 48:44.379
Well, for now,

48:44.463 --> 48:47.674
I'll ask the kids from the orphanage
I can get in touch with.

48:49.259 --> 48:51.053
That's a great idea.

49:01.229 --> 49:03.482
It's the finals for the three-legged race.

49:03.565 --> 49:05.484
Mr. Paik and Hong Hee-joo

49:05.567 --> 49:07.944
versus Jeong Won-bin and Ahn Jin-hee.

49:08.028 --> 49:11.114
Who will be the winning team?

49:15.535 --> 49:17.663
And they're off! Team Paik!

49:17.746 --> 49:20.582
They're running neck-and-neck!

49:20.666 --> 49:22.959
- Be careful!
- Go, Mr. Paik!

49:23.043 --> 49:24.127
Anyone, just win!

49:24.211 --> 49:26.588
- Good luck!
- That's a three-legged race!

49:26.672 --> 49:29.758
Won-bin's team is slowing down!
The finish line is just ahead!

49:29.841 --> 49:31.843
And they're down! Team Paik!

49:39.893 --> 49:41.186
Team Paik wins!

49:41.269 --> 49:43.647
Paik Sa-eon! Hong Hee-joo!

49:43.730 --> 49:46.858
- Paik Sa-eon! Hong Hee-joo!
- Paik Sa-eon!

50:00.664 --> 50:02.624
I'm sorry. I got carried away.

50:05.585 --> 50:06.420
Okay.

50:07.254 --> 50:08.422
Anyway, congrats!

50:08.505 --> 50:10.841
What prize should we prepare
for the winning team?

50:10.924 --> 50:12.467
Tell me if you want something.

50:12.551 --> 50:14.886
There is something I want.

50:17.514 --> 50:21.435
The weather's nice. The angle's nice.

50:21.518 --> 50:22.602
And the models…

50:23.687 --> 50:26.606
Did you two fight already?

50:26.690 --> 50:28.775
Can you move closer together?

50:29.735 --> 50:31.820
Yes, that's good.

50:32.654 --> 50:35.574
But is one photo really enough?

50:35.657 --> 50:37.576
I mean, it's your first place prize.

50:37.659 --> 50:39.536
There's meat and rice.

50:39.619 --> 50:40.704
I don't need it.

50:41.538 --> 50:43.874
A souvenir photo will be enough.

50:44.541 --> 50:46.418
Okay, then.

50:47.085 --> 50:47.919
Now.

50:48.003 --> 50:49.087
Smile.

50:50.922 --> 50:52.257
Bigger!

50:55.218 --> 50:56.052
That's good.

50:56.136 --> 50:58.305
Now… Tilt your head.

50:59.014 --> 51:00.807
Tilt. No, towards the middle, Mr. Paik.

51:00.891 --> 51:03.351
There you go. That's good. That's perfect!

51:03.435 --> 51:04.936
Good. Don't move.

51:05.479 --> 51:06.396
Make a hand heart.

51:33.590 --> 51:34.508
That's great.

51:35.550 --> 51:36.384
Now.

51:36.468 --> 51:37.511
I'll take it now.

51:37.594 --> 51:38.428
Good.

51:38.512 --> 51:39.930
Smile!

51:52.567 --> 51:53.693
Wait.

51:53.777 --> 51:54.861
Let's rest.

51:55.654 --> 51:57.364
Let's rest for a little.

51:57.447 --> 51:59.449
But you're dressed for the Himalayas.

52:00.283 --> 52:01.451
Yeah.

52:01.535 --> 52:03.829
Why did you want to hike this mountain?

52:03.912 --> 52:05.831
Did I suggest it? Did I?

52:06.581 --> 52:09.167
That man flying up there did.

52:10.168 --> 52:11.670
Wow, well…

52:11.753 --> 52:14.089
Can you believe Hong Hee-joo's stamina?

52:14.172 --> 52:15.257
It's unexpected.

52:15.340 --> 52:16.925
It's not just her stamina.

52:17.008 --> 52:19.427
Don't those two have good chemistry?

52:19.511 --> 52:20.554
I felt it too.

52:20.637 --> 52:21.847
During the three-legged race,

52:21.930 --> 52:23.014
- they were so in sync.
- Yes!

52:23.098 --> 52:24.391
He's a married man!

52:24.474 --> 52:25.725
You scared me!

52:25.809 --> 52:27.978
You said it before too.

52:28.061 --> 52:31.439
That sparks flew between the two
on the day of the interview.

52:31.523 --> 52:32.732
- When did I?
- Goodness.

52:32.816 --> 52:35.527
That's enough nonsense. Help me up.

52:36.736 --> 52:38.613
Here. One, two!

53:25.869 --> 53:27.245
Is that shirt all you have?

53:46.306 --> 53:48.016
It's cold once the sweat dries.

53:48.099 --> 53:49.392
Wear it later.

53:56.441 --> 53:59.903
- Where'd you buy your hiking clothes?
- That's not the issue right now.

54:00.779 --> 54:02.155
You dressed up the most.

54:02.238 --> 54:03.239
Over here.

54:03.323 --> 54:05.241
Who's the youngest among us?

54:05.325 --> 54:07.077
Me. I am.

54:25.178 --> 54:26.513
It's so pretty.

54:41.611 --> 54:42.779
We're here.

54:46.908 --> 54:47.951
It's beautiful.

54:50.662 --> 54:51.496
Hee-joo.

54:51.579 --> 54:53.206
Shall we take a photo together?

54:53.289 --> 54:54.457
- Yeah.
- Sounds good.

54:57.043 --> 54:59.379
One, two, three.

55:01.506 --> 55:04.050
Great job, everyone.

55:04.134 --> 55:06.386
Come and gather. Let's take a group photo.

55:06.469 --> 55:07.887
Here's the banner.

55:08.722 --> 55:10.015
Hold that up.

55:10.598 --> 55:11.725
Rows of two?

55:13.935 --> 55:14.769
Okay, behind.

55:14.853 --> 55:16.187
Don't push in the back.

55:16.271 --> 55:18.982
You'll be gone for good
if you fall, got it?

55:19.607 --> 55:20.442
Now.

55:20.525 --> 55:22.610
Okay, that's good. Gather together.

55:26.698 --> 55:28.241
Get closer.

55:28.324 --> 55:30.410
- Closer.
- Okay, that's good.

55:30.493 --> 55:31.453
Look at that.

55:31.536 --> 55:33.872
Isn't that Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon?

55:33.955 --> 55:36.207
- That's right.
- It is him!

55:36.291 --> 55:38.418
- Let us take a photo.
- You're so handsome!

55:39.544 --> 55:40.378
Just a moment.

55:40.462 --> 55:42.756
- Can we take a photo with you?
- After ours.

55:42.839 --> 55:44.382
Wait a moment.

55:44.466 --> 55:47.218
Just a moment. Please, don't push.

55:47.302 --> 55:48.762
Please maintain order.

55:49.345 --> 55:50.221
Just a moment.

55:51.222 --> 55:52.182
Mr. Park.

55:52.265 --> 55:55.185
People, please don't push. Maintain order.

55:56.144 --> 55:56.978
Mr. Park! Mr. Paik!

56:04.069 --> 56:04.986
Excuse me!

56:06.446 --> 56:07.530
Oh, no!

56:07.614 --> 56:09.365
- What do we do?
- What is it?

56:09.449 --> 56:11.201
A person fell.

56:11.868 --> 56:13.369
- Who?
- Hong Hee-joo.

56:13.453 --> 56:15.663
It happened in the blink of an eye.
Down the cliff.

56:16.331 --> 56:17.874
Step back. Please, step back.

56:17.957 --> 56:18.875
Hong Hee-joo.

56:19.584 --> 56:21.252
Hong Hee-joo!

56:44.484 --> 56:46.820
We were just about to take a group photo,

56:47.570 --> 56:49.155
and some hikers approached us.

56:49.239 --> 56:51.533
They barged in and started pushing.

56:51.616 --> 56:53.368
First, deploy the rescue team.

56:54.160 --> 56:56.329
It's almost 6 p.m.
It'll be bad if it gets dark.

56:56.412 --> 56:57.330
Mr. Paik!

57:08.675 --> 57:10.176
How did he come from there?

57:10.260 --> 57:12.095
He went down before you got here.

57:12.178 --> 57:14.264
- Down there?
- Are you okay? Were you hurt?

57:14.347 --> 57:16.516
How could you go down there like that?

57:16.599 --> 57:18.601
I saw a broken tree.

57:19.269 --> 57:21.563
I think she hit that on her way down.

57:21.646 --> 57:23.648
Can we deploy the rescue dogs right away?

57:23.731 --> 57:26.693
Yes, but we don't have
the missing person's belongings.

57:29.362 --> 57:31.114
They can smell this.

57:31.197 --> 57:33.575
She has my jacket around her waist. Hurry.

57:35.493 --> 57:37.078
Did you get through?

57:37.162 --> 57:38.246
No, I can't get through.

57:44.669 --> 57:45.753
HONG HEE-JOO

57:50.008 --> 57:52.051
The number you have dialed is…

57:55.680 --> 57:58.391
The number you have dialed is…

59:16.010 --> 59:18.012
Mr. Paik. Over here.

59:19.180 --> 59:22.141
People, please don't push. Maintain order.

59:26.312 --> 59:27.188
Someone…

01:00:30.585 --> 01:00:31.544
Sis?

01:00:32.337 --> 01:00:35.089
Do you know what kind of phone this is?

01:00:35.173 --> 01:00:36.341
This…

01:00:37.300 --> 01:00:39.177
can only call Paik Sa-eon.

01:00:39.260 --> 01:00:40.678
That was really true?

01:00:42.597 --> 01:00:44.349
Why is he so meticulous?

01:00:49.896 --> 01:00:50.897
Hong Hee-joo!

01:00:55.735 --> 01:00:56.569
Hong Hee-joo!

01:00:58.696 --> 01:00:59.697
PARK DO-JAE

01:01:01.157 --> 01:01:03.660
- What happened?
- They're still searching.

01:01:03.743 --> 01:01:07.580
They're searching up to 300 meters
downstream of the cliff, but…

01:01:08.414 --> 01:01:09.499
NBN KANG TAE-KYEONG

01:01:10.792 --> 01:01:14.045
Reporters keep calling me.
Has it already spread to the media?

01:01:14.128 --> 01:01:16.714
I'll regulate it.
And I'll expand the search radius.

01:01:16.798 --> 01:01:18.758
What about the security footage?

01:01:18.841 --> 01:01:21.719
The police are checking the footage
near the trail and summit.

01:01:21.803 --> 01:01:25.098
Our team members and people,
who were nearby when it happened,

01:01:25.181 --> 01:01:27.892
- are being questioned as witnesses.
- If you find anything,

01:01:27.975 --> 01:01:29.143
call me right away.

01:01:34.440 --> 01:01:35.775
CHUGYEONG DAILY NEWS PARK GUK-JIN

01:01:38.820 --> 01:01:40.154
Are you going to get that?

01:01:41.072 --> 01:01:42.198
No, I'm not.

01:01:44.909 --> 01:01:47.286
Because there's a call I'm waiting for.

01:02:04.262 --> 01:02:06.806
Are they conducting a search?

01:02:08.516 --> 01:02:10.268
Why don't I hear anything?

01:02:11.644 --> 01:02:15.565
Shouldn't there be helicopters
and drones looking for me?

01:02:26.075 --> 01:02:27.660
Is this how I'll get caught?

01:02:30.121 --> 01:02:31.372
I'm being punished.

01:02:32.582 --> 01:02:34.834
I should've confessed earlier.

01:02:36.627 --> 01:02:39.464
Yeah, it's for the best.

01:02:39.547 --> 01:02:41.632
I'll finally say it to him now.

01:02:44.051 --> 01:02:45.052
Yeah.

01:02:46.053 --> 01:02:46.971
Yeah.

01:02:48.639 --> 01:02:50.308
He might not pick up.

01:02:50.391 --> 01:02:51.559
No.

01:02:52.393 --> 01:02:55.313
It's over if he doesn't.
I need to snap out of it!

01:02:55.396 --> 01:02:56.814
Get it together.

01:03:05.114 --> 01:03:10.077
PAIK SA-EON

01:03:10.161 --> 01:03:12.580
Pick up. No. Don't pick up.

01:03:13.748 --> 01:03:15.082
Pick up, please.

01:03:20.630 --> 01:03:21.714
Hong Hee-joo!

01:03:24.258 --> 01:03:25.510
Hong Hee-joo!

01:03:28.012 --> 01:03:29.180
Hong Hee-joo!

01:03:36.979 --> 01:03:37.939
Hee-joo.

01:03:39.440 --> 01:03:40.525
I mean…

01:03:41.484 --> 01:03:42.485
406.

01:03:43.277 --> 01:03:44.195
What about Hee-joo?

01:03:45.571 --> 01:03:46.739
How is she?

01:03:47.532 --> 01:03:50.785
Does he think we're together?

01:03:50.868 --> 01:03:53.371
406, can you hear me?

01:03:56.874 --> 01:03:59.126
You said to call when there's a corpse.

01:04:02.213 --> 01:04:03.714
That's why I called.

01:04:04.715 --> 01:04:05.883
Come take her.

01:04:09.136 --> 01:04:10.137
That's good.

01:04:11.681 --> 01:04:13.182
Thank you for calling me.

01:04:15.309 --> 01:04:16.811
Where did Hee-joo fall?

01:04:17.520 --> 01:04:18.855
Just tell me the location.

01:04:31.242 --> 01:04:32.535
I don't know.

01:04:32.618 --> 01:04:33.536
406!

01:04:34.370 --> 01:04:35.663
Listen to me carefully.

01:04:35.746 --> 01:04:39.166
I've put a first-aid kit
inside of Hee-joo's backpack.

01:04:39.250 --> 01:04:41.794
At the bottom of the kit,
there's a portable flare.

01:04:41.878 --> 01:04:44.171
You can ignite it by striking the top lid.

01:04:44.255 --> 01:04:46.299
I hope Hee-joo finds it and uses it.

01:04:47.758 --> 01:04:49.427
What do you think, 406?

01:04:50.177 --> 01:04:51.304
If Hee-joo wakes up,

01:04:53.014 --> 01:04:54.807
wouldn't she try to search for something?

01:05:06.861 --> 01:05:09.947
Are you scared?

01:05:10.031 --> 01:05:11.032
Me?

01:05:12.283 --> 01:05:14.660
What's there to be scared of?

01:05:15.745 --> 01:05:16.913
I'm…

01:05:20.207 --> 01:05:22.126
scared to death right now.

01:05:22.209 --> 01:05:24.003
PAIK SA-EON

01:05:55.534 --> 01:05:57.703
406!

01:05:59.038 --> 01:06:00.289
Are you there?

01:06:00.373 --> 01:06:01.374
Answer me!

01:06:02.458 --> 01:06:03.459
I can hear you.

01:06:10.758 --> 01:06:12.510
The temperature has dropped.

01:06:13.594 --> 01:06:16.347
Do you think Hee-joo's cold?

01:06:17.515 --> 01:06:19.892
I don't know if she's wearing my jacket.

01:06:20.726 --> 01:06:22.520
There's water in her backpack too.

01:06:22.603 --> 01:06:24.438
She can't get dehydrated.

01:06:25.898 --> 01:06:27.733
She needs to drink water.

01:06:37.576 --> 01:06:38.828
You did it.

01:06:39.578 --> 01:06:40.579
I can see it.

01:06:45.418 --> 01:06:47.169
Come quickly.

01:06:47.253 --> 01:06:49.171
I'm on my way. Don't hang up!

01:06:49.255 --> 01:06:51.173
And if you can,

01:06:51.757 --> 01:06:53.259
please tell Hee-joo

01:06:53.342 --> 01:06:54.552
not to worry.

01:06:55.344 --> 01:06:57.972
Tell her I'll be right there!

01:07:15.448 --> 01:07:18.367
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:07:22.705 --> 01:07:23.622
Tell me.

01:07:24.665 --> 01:07:27.334
I'll say it once,
so listen carefully, 406.

01:07:28.169 --> 01:07:29.920
My true feelings for Hee-joo…

01:07:30.004 --> 01:07:32.423
What are your true feelings?

01:07:33.340 --> 01:07:34.508
Tell me.

01:07:40.139 --> 01:07:41.307
I can't hear you.

01:07:45.561 --> 01:07:46.687
Hong Hee-joo.

01:07:48.773 --> 01:07:49.774
I like you.

01:08:55.923 --> 01:08:58.843
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:08:58.926 --> 01:09:01.178
Starting now, I want you
to answer my questions.

01:09:01.262 --> 01:09:03.097
The most important question.

01:09:03.180 --> 01:09:04.098
Did you see his face?

01:09:04.181 --> 01:09:05.224
I like it.

01:09:05.307 --> 01:09:07.351
I like feeling your heartbeat.

01:09:07.852 --> 01:09:10.187
Is he taking a shower? Why?

01:09:10.271 --> 01:09:11.939
We've already slept together.

01:09:12.022 --> 01:09:13.232
Is this real?

01:09:13.315 --> 01:09:14.775
I felt regretful.

01:09:14.859 --> 01:09:17.153
I don't think I've done enough for you.

01:09:17.236 --> 01:09:18.362
No, I mean just me!

01:09:18.445 --> 01:09:20.531
You should return my phone.

01:09:20.614 --> 01:09:21.907
I'm on my way. Open the door.

01:09:27.413 --> 01:09:29.415
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
